{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b7f3a2d1-4c5e-4a8b-9f1d-2e3c4b5a6d7e",
    "name": "Content Creation Platform",
    "description": "Complete API collection for the AI-powered video content creation platform.\n\n## Quick Start\n1. Import this collection AND `Local.postman_environment.json`\n2. Select the **Local** environment in Postman\n3. Set `keycloak_client_secret` (Keycloak Admin → Clients → editor-api → Credentials tab)\n4. Run **Get Token (Password Grant)** once — subsequent requests auto-refresh the token\n\n## Happy-Path Workflow\n1. **Upload Video** → auto-captures `video_id`\n2. Poll **Get Video Status** until `status == READY`\n3. **Get Latest Edit Plan** → auto-captures `plan_id` + `segment_id`\n4. Optionally **Patch** or **Revise** the plan\n5. **Approve Edit Plan** → auto-captures `render_job_id`\n6. Poll **Get Render Job Status** until `status == COMPLETE` — grab `output_url`\n\n## Auth\nCollection-level Bearer auth injects `{{access_token}}` on every request. The pre-request script auto-refreshes the token when it expires (30 s buffer).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{access_token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Skip auto-refresh for requests that are themselves auth calls",
          "const SKIP = ['Get Token', 'Refresh Token', 'Get Admin Token', 'Client Credentials', 'Logout', 'Introspect Token'];",
          "if (SKIP.some(n => (pm.info.requestName || '').includes(n))) return;",
          "",
          "const token  = pm.collectionVariables.get('access_token');",
          "const expiry = parseInt(pm.collectionVariables.get('token_expiry') || '0');",
          "if (token && Date.now() < expiry) return;",
          "",
          "const baseKC  = pm.collectionVariables.get('keycloak_url');",
          "const realm   = pm.collectionVariables.get('keycloak_realm');",
          "const cid     = pm.collectionVariables.get('keycloak_client_id');",
          "const secret  = pm.collectionVariables.get('keycloak_client_secret');",
          "const user    = pm.collectionVariables.get('admin_username');",
          "const pass    = pm.collectionVariables.get('admin_password');",
          "",
          "if (!secret) {",
          "  console.warn('[auto-refresh] keycloak_client_secret is empty — set it in the environment');",
          "  return;",
          "}",
          "",
          "pm.sendRequest({",
          "  url: `${baseKC}/realms/${realm}/protocol/openid-connect/token`,",
          "  method: 'POST',",
          "  header: { 'Content-Type': 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded' },",
          "  body: {",
          "    mode: 'urlencoded',",
          "    urlencoded: [",
          "      { key: 'grant_type',    value: 'password' },",
          "      { key: 'client_id',     value: cid        },",
          "      { key: 'client_secret', value: secret     },",
          "      { key: 'username',      value: user       },",
          "      { key: 'password',      value: pass       }",
          "    ]",
          "  }",
          "}, function(err, res) {",
          "  if (!err && res.code === 200) {",
          "    const b = res.json();",
          "    pm.collectionVariables.set('access_token',  b.access_token);",
          "    pm.collectionVariables.set('refresh_token', b.refresh_token || '');",
          "    pm.collectionVariables.set('token_expiry',  String(Date.now() + (b.expires_in - 30) * 1000));",
          "    console.log('[auto-refresh] Token refreshed, expires in', b.expires_in, 's');",
          "  } else {",
          "    console.warn('[auto-refresh] Failed — check keycloak_client_secret and credentials. Code:', res && res.code);",
          "  }",
          "});"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
